A steel sphere of mass $0.29\text{ kg}$ is suspended in equilibrium from a vertical spring. The centre of the sphere is $8.5\text{ cm}$ from the top of the spring, as shown in Fig. 2.1.

{{figure:figure_2_1.png}}

The sphere is now set in motion so that it is moving in a horizontal circle at constant speed, as shown in Fig. 2.2.

{{figure:figure_2_2.png}}

The distance from the centre of the sphere to the top of the spring is now $10.8\text{ cm}$.
